WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:03.770
Some see it as the ultimate selfless act

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:07.507
Emma was potentially losing her life...

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.074
...on the table

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:12.112
But surrogacy—carrying a child for someone else...

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:15.115
...is also a fast-growing global trade...

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.718
...one that’s transforming ideas about family

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:22.222
The legal definition of family is changing over time

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.057
What’s driving this boom...

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.792
...in the baby business?

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:30.430
I’ve done, I believe, over 8,000 surrogate cycles in my career

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.400
...outlawed and hated in many countries

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.301
The inside of a woman’s body...

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:36.970
...is being used as a workplace

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:40.573
How can surrogacy be better policed...

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.043
...and its children better protected?

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.461
Good morning

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.463
Hi, how are you?

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.366
I’m feeling excited, a little bit nervous

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.935
Jessica has signed up...

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.336
...to provide the gift of life

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.173
This is just giving us permission...

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.809
...to place the embryo into your uterus

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.945
Just print, sign and date right there

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.248
Jessica is a surrogate

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.250
And she has no genetic link to the embryo...

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.352
...which is about to be implanted into her

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.522
I love being able to help someone...

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.391
...to be able to have a family...

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:34.327
...that they’re not able to on their own

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:38.465
Gestational surrogacy, as it’s known...

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.233
...is now significantly more common...

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.769
...than surrogates using their own eggs

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.539
Jessica’s doctor, David Smotrich...

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.575
...is one of its leading practitioners

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:53.079
Those of us who do a lot of surrogacy...

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:56.516
...find that gestational surrogacy is a better approach...

00:01:56.516 --> 00:02:00.587
...and it makes it much easier in terms of everybody involved

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:04.557
The genetic makeup of the child is something that is very...

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.893
...very concerning for the overwhelming...

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:08.795
...majority of couples that we work with

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.065
Jessica has had to pass stringent...

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.634
...medical and psychological vetting procedures

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.737
Who is driving you home today?

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.372
My husband will be picking me up

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.306
Okay

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.676
And most Californian agencies...

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.045
...require surrogates to be mothers already

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.783
For my kids, I’ve always told them, “Mom’s babysitting”

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.519
So they have always known that...

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.221
...the baby that I’m carrying is not ours

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.890
So we’re going to take you back...

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.725
...and just get started, okay?

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:39.492
Showtime!

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.095
All the testing that we’re doing on her and her body...

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.564
...actually is for another couple

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.739
All righty!

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.440
It’s nice that they’re awake!

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.847
That couple are Nima and Hamish

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:04.450
Based in Australia, they are the “intended parents” as they’re often called

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.521
In Australia, it’s very difficult to adopt

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.191
Surrogacy sort of felt like really the only...

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.927
...reliable option in terms of having a child

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:17.830
The embryo implanted inside Jessica...

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.732
...was made using Nima’s sperm...

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.235
...and an egg from an American donor

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.637
Hello!

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:28.541
Jessica has already given the couple a son, Hugo

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:33.012
Now they’re hoping she’ll add a baby girl to the family

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.480
Jessica, are you ready?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.081
I’m ready

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:38.051
Okay, you’re going to feel my fingertips first and then speculum

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.385
Okay? Here we go

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.655
California...

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:45.758
...so often at the forefront of new technologies...

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.228
...has become the surrogacy capital of the world

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:54.400
I’ve done, I believe, over 8,000 surrogate cycles in my career

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.936
We’ve helped couples in over 100 different countries...

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.638
...become families

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.707
If you look at the screen behind me...

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:01.841
...we’re going to show you...

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:04.477
...the actual embryo that we are going to transfer

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.348
Back in 1998...

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:11.484
...David was one of the first doctors to help same-sex couples...

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:14.621
...become parents through surrogacy

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.624
This is my trial catheter

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.328
Okay, I’m covering you up

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:27.700
Some may say you can’t put a price on having a family

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.669
But here in California, they do

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.607
Intended parents usually pay between $110,000...

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:39.345
...to upwards of $200,000 for surrogacy services

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.180
And surrogates like Jessica...

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.684
...can earn between $30,000 and $60,000

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.986
Do you want to stop and make your appointment for Monday?

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.388
Yes

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.156
When you’re a first-time surrogate...

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:53.526
...you obviously don’t know if IVF is going to work for you

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:57.830
So as you go on to a second one, the pay increases...

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.601
...because obviously they know that you can carry this baby...

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.969
...with no issues

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:07.006
Think about everything that we are putting our body through...

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.709
...to be able to have this baby

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:14.213
For Nima, the transactional nature of the relationship...

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:17.483
...with Jessica is part of the appeal

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.118
I see it as a win-win

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:22.055
She is doing something amazing for us...

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:24.424
...able to earn some money through it...

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:28.561
...to help her own family and has made the decision herself

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.230
Bye bye!

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:39.238
The number of children born to surrogacy globally is unknown

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:42.342
Data only exist for some countries, such as Britain

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:48.281
And this shows a small but increasing number of parental orders...

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:51.617
...transfers of custodial rights from surrogates to intended parents

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:57.123
But globally, the surrogacy industry was estimated to be worth...

00:05:57.123 --> 00:06:00.293
...over $14bn in 2022...

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:03.730
...a figure that may rise as high as $130bn...

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.965
...over the coming decade

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.369
Same-sex couples wanting children...

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:11.371
...are one of the key drivers of this growth

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:16.676
In Britain, for example, about half of all intended parents are gay

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.580
The legal definition of family...

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.248
...is changing over time

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:23.583
Which means that the definition...

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:26.786
...of family is now accepted...

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:28.454
...as being more than just the...

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.923
...you know, mum, dad and 2.5 children

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:34.994
But there’s another, perhaps more significant factor...

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.896
...making the surrogacy business grow

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:43.603
Declining fertility rates amongst the heterosexual population

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:48.374
Women are now choosing to start families later in life...

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:51.077
...and this carries a higher risk of infertility

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.913
The World Health Organisation recently...

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:56.349
...produced a report that said up to...

00:06:56.349 --> 00:07:01.487
...17.5% of people will be affected by infertility in their lives

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:03.189
So that’s one in six people

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:07.427
So if you are infertile, if you have a burning desire...

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:10.830
...to have a family, you generally have tried everything else...

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:14.534
...you’ve tried IVF, your last resort is surrogacy

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:21.107
The surrogacy industry has also benefited from celebrity limelight

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:26.646
As the Paris Hiltons of this world keep up with the likes of Khloe Kardashian

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:29.982
When I went to the hospital, I really think that was the first time...

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:31.150
...that it really registered

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.952
You’re like, “Okay, we’re having a baby!”

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:37.256
Even if such famous parents are usually living...

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.625
...in a different financial reality from most

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:42.895
Well, it might be inspiring...

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:43.729
...and it’s news 

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:46.632
It’s certainly not the norm for most people going through these processes...

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.434
...who haven’t got the money or the status

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:55.308
What’s especially striking about the surrogacy business...

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:58.778
...is how globalised it’s become

00:07:58.778 --> 00:08:00.279
Here’s why

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:03.583
Relatively few countries allow surrogates to be expressly paid...

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:05.485
...for the labour of carrying a child

00:08:08.321 --> 00:08:12.625
For example, Georgia, Ukraine and certain states in America 

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:16.028
However, this kind of commercial surrogacy...

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:18.164
...is against the law in many more countries...

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:22.201
...like China, Germany, Turkey, France...

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:25.638
...and Italy

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:30.943
That means residents of these countries wanting a surrogate have to look abroad...

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:33.846
...to countries where surrogacy is allowed

00:08:40.052 --> 00:08:43.656
The transnational business of surrogacy is very fluid

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:46.259
Originally, India was a popular destination

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:49.462
The Indian government then said, “No, we’re not going to allow foreigners...

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:52.865
...to come in and use our population for surrogacy”

00:08:52.865 --> 00:08:55.167
And it was shut down in Thailand

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.202
Then it went to Laos

00:08:56.936 --> 00:09:00.606
We’re seeing an increasing trend for countries in Europe particularly...

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.842
...to turn their laws against surrogacy...

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:04.877
...and to forbid their citizens from engaging in it

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:13.553
Opposition to surrogacy often comes from the religious right...

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:15.054
...and conservative politicians

00:09:15.655 --> 00:09:16.722
In Italy...

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:20.126
...one politician has even compared surrogacy to child abuse

00:09:20.126 --> 00:09:24.263
It’s a serious crime, in my opinion more serious than paedophilia

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:27.466
On the other side of the political spectrum...

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:30.503
...radical feminists are often equally opposed...

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:32.805
...if for different reasons

00:09:32.805 --> 00:09:34.307
It’s a financial trade...

00:09:34.307 --> 00:09:37.009
...therefore, there’s huge amounts of exploitation...

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:41.080
...because the inside of a woman’s body is being used as a workplace

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:46.185
It’s not just hostility and laws...

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:49.755
...which push intended parents to seek surrogates overseas

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:51.424
It’s hard economics, too

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:55.761
For those unable to afford services in America...

00:09:55.761 --> 00:09:58.264
...other countries offer lower-cost alternatives

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:03.402
In Greece, prices start at around $88,000...

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:05.771
...while in Georgia, it’s less than half that...

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:13.112
...although in 2024, foreigners will be banned from surrogacy services there

00:10:17.683 --> 00:10:19.518
Before the Russian invasion...

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:22.488
...Ukraine was a global surrogacy hub...

00:10:22.488 --> 00:10:27.560
...offering affordable prices to customers from rich countries

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.228
Ukraine, almost by accident...

00:10:29.228 --> 00:10:30.396
...had laws...

00:10:30.396 --> 00:10:33.833
...that allowed foreigners to be named on the birth certificate

00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:37.703
There was a large number of high-quality IVF clinics popped up

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:39.505
It also has a very large population...

00:10:39.505 --> 00:10:41.440
...so there was no shortage of surrogates...

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.908
...to meet that demand

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:47.613
There are babies from America, Italy, Spain...

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:51.784
...Britain, China, France and Germany, as well as from Bulgaria

00:10:51.784 --> 00:10:56.789
Before the war, Ukrainian surrogates were producing over 2,500 babies...

00:10:56.789 --> 00:10:59.058
...each year, mostly for foreigners...

00:11:00.593 --> 00:11:02.862
...with half of that demand coming from China...

00:11:02.862 --> 00:11:04.697
...where surrogacy is banned

00:11:09.468 --> 00:11:12.071
The war has since reduced demand...

00:11:12.071 --> 00:11:16.509
...although it’s also forced aspiring parents to take unusual measures

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:20.713
People will go to extreme lengths to be united with their child

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.716
Wealthier returning parents were engaging...

00:11:23.716 --> 00:11:25.918
...security teams with armoured vehicles...

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:27.586
...to take them into Ukraine, into Kyiv...

00:11:27.586 --> 00:11:29.288
...to pick up their baby and take them out

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.391
The rise in IVF...

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.860
...cheap air travel and online marketing...

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:39.799
...have all allowed low-cost surrogacy agencies to expand across the world

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.970
But there is a dark underbelly to this industry

00:11:45.304 --> 00:11:49.742
In countries as widespread as Guatemala, Laos and Kenya...

00:11:49.742 --> 00:11:53.312
...surrogacy is neither banned nor permitted under law

00:11:53.312 --> 00:11:56.649
In these places, the industry is unregulated...

00:11:56.649 --> 00:11:58.918
...and raising concerns

00:11:58.918 --> 00:12:00.986
The surrogacy industry, it’s really growing...

00:12:00.986 --> 00:12:03.389
...and it’s growing so fast

00:12:04.256 --> 00:12:07.326
Naipanoi Lepapa is a journalist in Nairobi...

00:12:07.326 --> 00:12:11.897
...who exposes the human cost of failing to regulate surrogacy

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:14.166
If you use surrogates in my country...

00:12:14.166 --> 00:12:16.669
...there are no laws around this practice

00:12:16.669 --> 00:12:22.007
This means surrogates are not protected and some are exploited

00:12:22.475 --> 00:12:25.778
I have met surrogates who have been intimidated...

00:12:25.778 --> 00:12:28.247
...who have been forced to have abortions...

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:32.384
...and then they are defrauded out of their money

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:42.895
In a country where 27% of the population lives below the poverty line...

00:12:42.895 --> 00:12:45.498
...of just over $2 a day...

00:12:45.498 --> 00:12:49.168
...agencies prey on vulnerable and illiterate women in slums...

00:12:49.168 --> 00:12:51.337
...like this one in Dandora

00:12:52.371 --> 00:12:54.640
 Naipanoi discovered one victim...

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.642
...who miscarried at five months...

00:12:56.642 --> 00:12:59.745
...but was left with the dead foetus inside her for days...

00:12:59.745 --> 00:13:02.448
...and left crippled for life

00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:05.851
Instead of immediately removing the foetus...

00:13:05.851 --> 00:13:08.087
...the agent told her he’s going to look...

00:13:08.087 --> 00:13:10.389
...for someone who is going to operate on her

00:13:10.389 --> 00:13:12.057
So it took a whole week

00:13:12.892 --> 00:13:15.427
She’s always in pain, she can’t do anything

00:13:15.427 --> 00:13:16.962
She’s still struggling

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:20.099
To add insult to injury...

00:13:20.099 --> 00:13:23.102
...this surrogate was never even paid

00:13:23.102 --> 00:13:25.304
You only get paid when you produce a baby...

00:13:25.304 --> 00:13:27.306
...but when you miscarried, you’re not paid anything

00:13:32.411 --> 00:13:35.281
Naipanoi is on her way to meet another victim 

00:13:36.182 --> 00:13:38.584
Today I’m meeting a woman...

00:13:38.584 --> 00:13:44.390
...who says she was asked for sex in exchange for work...

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.058
...as a surrogate

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.461
This woman agreed to be filmed...

00:13:49.461 --> 00:13:51.463
...provided her identity is protected

00:13:52.631 --> 00:13:56.802
Some surrogates have said that they have been asked for sex

00:13:56.802 --> 00:13:59.972
Did it also happen to you?

00:13:59.972 --> 00:14:03.576
Yes, it happened to me, yes

00:14:03.576 --> 00:14:06.212
And I came to realise that that man...

00:14:06.212 --> 00:14:09.615
...is sleeping with almost every girl

00:14:09.615 --> 00:14:12.084
Since I had no option...

00:14:12.084 --> 00:14:13.886
...I did it because he was promising me...

00:14:13.886 --> 00:14:16.722
...he was going to shape my life

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:21.060
She was recruited as a surrogate through Facebook...

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:25.030
...and was promised a life-changing $4,500...

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:27.199
...roughly two years’ earnings

00:14:27.199 --> 00:14:30.469
But she was given no medical advice

00:14:30.469 --> 00:14:32.738
They didn’t ask me to sign anything...

00:14:32.738 --> 00:14:34.807
...before the embryo transfer...

00:14:34.807 --> 00:14:37.142
...so I was not concerned about all those things 

00:14:37.142 --> 00:14:40.145
All I was praying for is that the process goes through well...

00:14:40.145 --> 00:14:42.882
...and I get pregnant so I can get the money

00:14:44.049 --> 00:14:48.153
It is considered good practice to transfer only one embryo...

00:14:48.153 --> 00:14:52.091
...to reduce the risks to both mother and baby

00:14:52.091 --> 00:14:55.728
This woman endured the transfer of four embryos...

00:14:55.728 --> 00:14:57.596
...without choice

00:14:57.596 --> 00:15:00.799
Three of the embryos implanted successfully...

00:15:00.799 --> 00:15:05.671
...and rather than risk triplets, the agency chose to abort one

00:15:05.671 --> 00:15:08.574
She was later forced to have a Caesarean section...

00:15:08.574 --> 00:15:10.209
...to deliver twins... 

00:15:10.209 --> 00:15:13.345
...and is still owed over half her money

00:15:14.513 --> 00:15:16.181
They operated on me

00:15:16.181 --> 00:15:18.751
I felt like running away

00:15:18.751 --> 00:15:20.953
I’ve never experienced that kind of pain

00:15:20.953 --> 00:15:23.856
I couldn’t move, I couldn’t do anything

00:15:23.856 --> 00:15:27.660
Why do you think CS [caesarean sections] are performed on surrogates?

00:15:28.394 --> 00:15:30.930
They don’t care about surrogates

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:34.400
They just want to remove their babies

00:15:35.801 --> 00:15:40.039
Life is much riskier for surrogates in poor countries like Kenya...

00:15:40.039 --> 00:15:42.875
...where for every 100,000 births...

00:15:42.875 --> 00:15:46.078
...an estimated 530 women die

00:15:46.078 --> 00:15:50.916
By comparison, in the EU, that figure is just 6

00:15:54.053 --> 00:15:59.792
The surrogacy market within poor countries is often driven by foreign demand

00:15:59.792 --> 00:16:03.362
So what, if anything, can be done to address this...

00:16:03.362 --> 00:16:06.765
...global problem of exploitation of surrogates?

00:16:06.765 --> 00:16:09.835
Banning surrogacy is not the answer

00:16:09.835 --> 00:16:13.505
Just as human rights law says, you cannot tell a woman...

00:16:13.505 --> 00:16:16.909
...that she has to have an abortion or that she can’t have an abortion...

00:16:16.909 --> 00:16:19.244
...the same principles apply to surrogacy

00:16:19.244 --> 00:16:21.914
It is the individual woman’s choice...

00:16:21.914 --> 00:16:25.417
...whether and how she uses her reproductive system

00:16:26.418 --> 00:16:29.788
Perhaps a better idea would be to make surrogacy legal...

00:16:29.788 --> 00:16:32.224
...and well regulated in more places

00:16:32.224 --> 00:16:35.427
The fact that surrogacy is such a transnational business...

00:16:35.427 --> 00:16:36.628
...is very problematic

00:16:36.628 --> 00:16:39.231
It will be much better if countries could come to terms...

00:16:39.231 --> 00:16:41.834
...with the fact that their nationals do require surrogacy...

00:16:41.834 --> 00:16:44.470
...and they could put laws in place in their own countries...

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.939
...to allow much easier access to surrogacy at home

00:16:51.844 --> 00:16:52.911
In Britain...

00:16:52.911 --> 00:16:55.981
...one survey found that two-thirds of intended parents...

00:16:55.981 --> 00:16:58.417
...chose to go overseas for surrogacy...

00:16:58.417 --> 00:17:01.587
...because they felt laws were unfavourable to them at home

00:17:03.956 --> 00:17:06.792
After birth, it can take half a year...

00:17:06.792 --> 00:17:12.064
...or more for intended parents to become legal guardians of their surrogate children

00:17:15.401 --> 00:17:17.102
How many shirts are you bringing?

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.438
Erm...three?

00:17:20.005 --> 00:17:22.541
Campaigners like Alan White and his partner Nic...

00:17:22.541 --> 00:17:26.712
...have contributed to law reforms that will make this process quicker

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.883
Alan is chair of the board of SurrogacyUK...

00:17:30.883 --> 00:17:34.219
...a non-profit advocacy and support group

00:17:35.721 --> 00:17:39.091
The law changes will make things more secure...

00:17:39.091 --> 00:17:41.360
...for all parties involved in surrogacy

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.595
Surrogates, under the current law...

00:17:43.595 --> 00:17:46.832
...they are the legal parents of a child born through surrogacy...

00:17:46.832 --> 00:17:49.501
...so actually, they carry a tremendous amount of risk in the process

00:17:49.501 --> 00:17:50.836
Oh what’s up with you?

00:17:51.737 --> 00:17:55.040
It is a bit bonkers in comparison to other people’s experience...

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:56.975
...that you wouldn’t expect someone to turn up...

00:17:56.975 --> 00:17:58.644
...when your child’s six months old...

00:17:58.644 --> 00:18:01.380
...and decide whether you can keep him or not

00:18:02.781 --> 00:18:03.415
What was that?

00:18:03.415 --> 00:18:04.450
Broccoli

00:18:04.883 --> 00:18:06.251
Are you messy?

00:18:07.686 --> 00:18:11.423
The couple are about to take their surrogate-born child, Jago...

00:18:11.423 --> 00:18:13.358
...on holiday for the first time

00:18:13.358 --> 00:18:15.060
Let’s go, let’s go, let’s go

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:20.132
But even though he is five months old, Jago is still legally not their child

00:18:20.132 --> 00:18:21.366
Don’t eat your feet

00:18:22.968 --> 00:18:23.969
I think you look nice

00:18:26.371 --> 00:18:29.374
Until a parental order is granted by the courts...

00:18:29.374 --> 00:18:35.214
...in legal terms, Jago’s surrogate, Emma, will be left holding the baby

00:18:35.214 --> 00:18:37.549
So you’d sit him between your legs and need to put some toys in front of him

00:18:37.549 --> 00:18:41.019
I knew I was legally his parent, and I knew that my husband...

00:18:41.019 --> 00:18:43.388
...he would have to go on the birth certificate...

00:18:43.388 --> 00:18:45.457
...which is completely not right either

00:18:48.093 --> 00:18:51.530
In Britain, surrogates like Emma cannot be paid...

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.333
...but can receive pregnancy-related expenses

00:18:55.601 --> 00:18:58.837
It’s sometimes known as the altruistic model...

00:18:58.837 --> 00:19:00.172
...and in Emma’s case...

00:19:00.172 --> 00:19:04.543
...it may be hard to find a worthier example of that term

00:19:04.543 --> 00:19:08.213
I ended up delivering Jago, and then immediately after...

00:19:08.213 --> 00:19:11.383
...bled quite a lot, so I had to be rushed to theatre

00:19:12.217 --> 00:19:15.354
After the birth, Emma had a big postpartum haemorrhage

00:19:15.354 --> 00:19:18.857
The room suddenly filled with 20 medical staff...

00:19:18.857 --> 00:19:21.360
...crash trolleys, all the stuff that you don’t want to see

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:25.097
Emma was potentially losing her life on the table

00:19:25.764 --> 00:19:28.767
The midwifery team started talking to Emma about having to do things...

00:19:28.767 --> 00:19:30.502
...to save her life, and it was horrible

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:35.741
Emma’s six children and her husband nearly lost her

00:19:35.741 --> 00:19:38.510
All so that Alan and Nic could become parents

00:19:40.646 --> 00:19:42.614
There’s no way you can thank someone for that...

00:19:42.614 --> 00:19:43.415
...you just can’t

00:19:43.415 --> 00:19:44.750
There just aren’t the words

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:47.853
Holding him for the first time and realising that this is your child...

00:19:47.853 --> 00:19:50.889
...that you’re responsible for his happiness, and...

00:19:50.889 --> 00:19:52.691
...it’s amazing

00:19:52.691 --> 00:19:54.259
Yeah, it is, it is

00:19:55.427 --> 00:19:59.598
I never saw it as a massive deal, to be honest

00:19:59.598 --> 00:20:01.967
To somebody else who couldn’t have children...

00:20:01.967 --> 00:20:05.103
...I’ve got all the bits to help, so why wouldn’t I help?

00:20:06.238 --> 00:20:10.943
As well as Britain, other countries using the altruistic model include...

00:20:10.943 --> 00:20:13.378
...Canada and Australia

00:20:13.378 --> 00:20:17.115
Supporters say forbidding surrogates to charge direct fees...

00:20:17.115 --> 00:20:22.921
...for childbearing reduces the risks of exploitation

00:20:22.921 --> 00:20:25.290
However, critics point out...

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:28.660
...the altruistic model is far from a catch-all solution...

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.729
 ...to global surrogacy’s problems

00:20:32.231 --> 00:20:34.533
When we look at who’s involved in surrogacy...

00:20:34.533 --> 00:20:38.837
...there’s generally lawyers, doctors, nurses...

00:20:38.837 --> 00:20:40.973
...and they are all getting paid for their services

00:20:40.973 --> 00:20:44.243
The only person who is not being paid for their services...

00:20:44.243 --> 00:20:47.546
...is the surrogate, who’s doing, let’s face it, most of the labour

00:20:47.546 --> 00:20:48.413
Pun intended

00:20:49.147 --> 00:20:51.750
I would like to see minimum and maximum amounts...

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:54.386
 ...of compensation for surrogacy

00:20:54.386 --> 00:20:56.688
Psychological evaluations of all the parties...

00:20:56.688 --> 00:20:59.124
...before they embark on surrogacy

00:20:59.124 --> 00:21:02.661
There should be mandatory requirements for legal advice

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:08.767
Regulating such a global business is an enormous challenge

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:13.805
And in the often heated debate about this...

00:21:13.805 --> 00:21:17.109
...the outcomes of surrogate children can sometimes get forgotten

00:21:17.976 --> 00:21:19.978
There is an argument that children...

00:21:19.978 --> 00:21:22.981
...born by surrogacy are somehow disadvantaged

00:21:22.981 --> 00:21:24.883
The research doesn’t support that

00:21:24.883 --> 00:21:27.853
We know that children born via surrogacy...

00:21:27.853 --> 00:21:30.555
...do as well as children born in other ways

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:34.426
A recent study suggests that telling surrogate-born children...

00:21:34.426 --> 00:21:37.029
...about their origins early in life can help

00:21:38.664 --> 00:21:42.467
7% of mothers who did this before their child turned seven...

00:21:42.467 --> 00:21:45.037
...reported problems in family relationships...

00:21:45.037 --> 00:21:49.775
...compared with 22% who disclosed after the age of seven

00:21:53.278 --> 00:21:56.848
So the aim is to hear your views on the surrogacy law

00:21:56.848 --> 00:21:59.584
At the University of Leicester, in Britain

00:21:59.584 --> 00:22:02.254
Dr Katherine Wade and her colleagues have analysed...

00:22:02.254 --> 00:22:05.157
...children’s views on surrogacy laws

00:22:05.157 --> 00:22:08.527
They gathered quantitative and qualitative information...

00:22:08.527 --> 00:22:11.797
...by talking to children born through surrogacy

00:22:11.797 --> 00:22:15.067
We wanted to stop this process of always making assumptions...

00:22:15.067 --> 00:22:16.168
...about how children might feel...

00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:17.736
...and actually ask them how they do feel

00:22:18.637 --> 00:22:23.041
This is a simulation of the team’s focus-group research

00:22:23.041 --> 00:22:26.345
Should children born through surrogacy be told that they were...

00:22:26.345 --> 00:22:28.146
...born this way?

00:22:28.146 --> 00:22:32.017
I put yes, you can discover a new part about yourself

00:22:32.617 --> 00:22:35.220
It’s good to know early because if you find out...

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:38.023
...you could get a bit angry at your parents for not telling you

00:22:38.323 --> 00:22:39.891
Be wondering why you weren’t told...

00:22:39.891 --> 00:22:41.893
...and wondering if there was something wrong...

00:22:41.893 --> 00:22:42.361
...with it

00:22:44.363 --> 00:22:47.532
In many countries, including Britain...

00:22:47.532 --> 00:22:51.636
...you can usually only find out the identities of your egg and sperm donors...

00:22:51.636 --> 00:22:55.273
...but not, in most cases, your surrogate

00:22:55.273 --> 00:22:56.608
Should children born...

00:22:56.608 --> 00:22:59.978
...through surrogacy know who their surrogate was?

00:22:59.978 --> 00:23:03.782
Yes, because you could be related to them

00:23:03.782 --> 00:23:05.183
There’s no reason to not know

00:23:05.183 --> 00:23:08.420
It’s just creating mysteries, it’s just creating a problem

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:09.821
 We have our surrogate in our lives...

00:23:09.821 --> 00:23:11.723
...and it’s nice to have them around

00:23:11.723 --> 00:23:14.025
It’s like a little bit of an extended family

00:23:14.793 --> 00:23:17.863
Although circumstances are different for individuals...

00:23:17.863 --> 00:23:21.032
...this information can help each to develop what is termed...

00:23:21.032 --> 00:23:23.402
...their narrative identity

00:23:24.002 --> 00:23:27.472
People are forming integrated life stories throughout their life

00:23:27.472 --> 00:23:29.474
It means that you should try to disclose...

00:23:29.474 --> 00:23:31.777
...this information to children throughout their childhood

00:23:33.278 --> 00:23:34.846
Katherine and her team’s research...

00:23:34.846 --> 00:23:38.583
...has fed into forthcoming reforms to laws in Britain

00:23:39.351 --> 00:23:42.220
This will include a mandatory register...

00:23:42.220 --> 00:23:44.055
...where from the age of 16...

00:23:44.055 --> 00:23:47.426
...you can trace nearly everything about your genetic origins...

00:23:47.426 --> 00:23:50.695
...from your surrogate to overseas donors

00:23:51.897 --> 00:23:55.434
Some states in Australia have a similar law

00:23:55.434 --> 00:23:59.304
That is the gold standard: when children can learn...

00:23:59.304 --> 00:24:01.606
...their genetic origin stories

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:07.446
What’s in the best interests of the child...

00:24:07.446 --> 00:24:09.481
...is a good starting point for thinking...

00:24:09.481 --> 00:24:12.884
...about how to better police the global surrogacy industry

00:24:14.519 --> 00:24:16.822
With demand rising rapidly...

00:24:16.822 --> 00:24:19.691
...getting surrogacy right matters more than ever

00:24:20.625 --> 00:24:22.527
We’re not going to be able to stop surrogacy...

00:24:22.527 --> 00:24:26.932
...so let’s instead regulate it so that it is...

00:24:26.932 --> 00:24:31.136
...a world-class system that respects the rights...

00:24:31.136 --> 00:24:32.904
...of all parties who are involved in it

00:24:59.831 --> 00:25:03.635
Hi I’m Mian Ridge a correspondent on The Economist’s Britain desk

00:25:03.635 --> 00:25:07.339
If you’d like to read more about surrogacy, please click on the link

00:25:07.339 --> 00:25:09.975
And if you’d like to watch more of our Now &amp; Next series...

00:25:09.975 --> 00:25:11.576
...please click on the other link

00:25:11.576 --> 00:25:14.079
Thanks for watching and please don’t forget to subscribe

